# appApple/.gitignore
#
# ELI5: Files XcodeGen/Xcode/SwiftPM regenerate every time, so we never
# commit them — commit `project.yml` (and the Swift sources) instead, and
# regenerate with `Scripts/bootstrap.sh`.
#
# DETAILED: Per strategy §1.1: "gitignore the generated .xcodeproj." The
# same reasoning extends to every other build-tool-generated artifact under
# `appApple/` — none of these are hand-authored, all of them are
# byte-for-byte reproducible from `project.yml` + the Swift sources, and
# committing them would just create merge-conflict noise with zero
# information content (a coding agent — or a human — reviewing a diff of a
# regenerated binary-ish `.xcodeproj` learns nothing `project.yml`'s own
# diff didn't already say more clearly).

# The Xcode project XcodeGen generates from project.yml.
*.xcodeproj/

# Per-user Xcode workspace state (breakpoints, window layout, ...) — never
# meaningful to another contributor or CI.
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate

# XcodeGen-generated Info.plist files (written fresh by `xcodegen generate`
# whenever a target's `info:` property is present — see iHymnsWidgets in
# project.yml).
Apps/**/Generated/

# SwiftPM build output for the iHymnsKit package (`swift build`/`swift
# test` artifacts) and its resolved-version lockfile churn during local
# iteration — `Package.resolved` itself IS worth committing for
# reproducible dependency resolution, so it is deliberately NOT listed here.
Packages/**/.build/
Packages/**/.swiftpm/

# Xcode's own DerivedData, if a contributor ever points it inside the repo
# instead of the default `~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData`.
DerivedData/

# Fastlane run artifacts (#1400) — `fastlane/Appfile`/`fastlane/Fastfile`
# ARE hand-authored and committed; everything below is written fresh by
# every `fastlane <lane>` run (locally or in CI) and carries zero review
# value as a diff.
fastlane/builds/
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/README.md
fastlane/test_output/

# macOS Finder noise.
.DS_Store
